cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark suite, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "disslucc-benchmark: Reproducible Validation of disslucc against the LuccME 3.1 Labs"
abstract: "Benchmark that runs disslucc on the LuccME functional labs and compares it, year by year and cell by cell, with the TerraME 2.0.1 goldens of luccme-goldens, reporting how much of LuccME the Python implementation reproduces."
version: 0.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-04
license: MIT
url: "https://github.com/LambdaGeo/disslucc-benchmark"
repository-code: "https://github.com/LambdaGeo/disslucc-benchmark"
keywords:
  - "land-use change"
  - "benchmarking"
  - "reproducibility"
  - "numerical parity"
  - "TerraME"
  - "LuccME"
  - "disslucc"
  - "open science"
authors:
